      "description": "Watch KAA Gent vs KV Mechelen highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League delivered a fascinating encounter on August 10, 2026, as KAA Gent hosted KV Mechelen . Both teams approached the match with high intensity, setting the stage for a clash defined by tactical discipline and clinical finishing. First-Half Blitz Defines the Game After a cagey opening period, KV Mechelen suffered an early setback when Gora Diouf was forced off in the 28th minute, replaced by Kobe Corbanie . KAA Gent soon capitalized on the shifting dynamics. In the 37th minute, the deadlock was broken as Tiago Araujo found the back of the net with a composed finish, putting the home side in the driver's seat. The pressure from the hosts didn't stop there. Just as the first half was drawing to a close in the 45th minute, Momodou Sonko turned provider with a brilliant assist for Josue Vergara . The forward made no mistake, doubling the lead and leaving the visitors with a mountain to climb. The referee eventually blew for half-time after six minutes of added time, with Gent firmly in control. Tactical Management and Final Whistle The second half began with KV Mechelen making a double substitution, introducing Malcolm Lohunanu-Mbasi and Maksim Paskotsi to spark a comeback. Despite the fresh legs, KAA Gent remained organized and professional. A series of further changes followed for both sides, including the introduction of Mathias Delorge and Hyllarion Goore as the coaches looked to manage the energy levels on the pitch. As the clock ticked down, the match grew more physical, leading to a yellow card for Massimo Decoene in the 85th minute. Gent safely navigated the final stages, including five minutes of stoppage time, to secure the three points. The final whistle confirmed a comprehensive performance from the hosts, who managed the game expertly after their first-half heroics."
